  "articleBody": "It's one thing for a ramp to show a little wear and tear, but if it's feeling wobbly or you're seeing actual damage, it's time to pay close attention. You might be wondering, \"Can I fix this myself, or do I need to call someone?\" Well, if you're dealing with structural damage, that's a big sign to get professional help. This isn't just about a loose screw; it's about the very integrity of the ramp. If you notice repeated movement, especially where the ramp connects to the building, or if the supports themselves are damaged, that's definitely a red flag. Anything that affects the ramp's load-bearing capacity or overall safety means it's gone beyond a simple DIY project. Remember, a ramp has to support weight safely, and if that's compromised, it becomes a serious fall risk. Don't take chances with safety! If you're seeing any of these issues in the Denver metro area, including places like Aurora, Centennial, or Highlands Ranch, give us a ring at HH Remodeling LLC. We've got the expertise to assess what's going on and make sure your ramp is safe and compliant. We're here to help get things fixed up properly.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
